If the door is just stuck, you can open it if you just keep using the o
command. But if it is LOCKED, you can NOT open it just with o, you need to
either use a key or lock pick or a wand/spell of opening, or kick it open.
And the same goes for chests and boxes.

> As far as chests go I don't think I have *ever* kicked one since I have
> been playing the game after reading posts of things shattering inside.

True, potions and glass wands in the chest/box may shatter if you kick the
container. But in the early game, when I haven't found any opening tool
yet, I still often kick the locked containers, even though I often hear
the shattering sound. I think that by the time I find a key/lock pick and
come back, a potion or two probably don't make too much difference
compared to getting the possible non-glass stuff out earlier. 
But this is a matter of taste / style, and YMMV.

